build: enable the focus motor driver in the board defconfig

Note: this diff is against a REPO file, not the kernel tree. Apply it with
-p1 from mainline/, not from the kernel build tree like the other patches
in this directory.

CONFIG_HY310_KEYSTONE_MOTOR has been "not set" since the driver was written,
so nothing in the shipping kernel has ever loaded it and none of its
behaviour has been exercised on the current tree. Build it, as a module
rather than built-in: its probe queues a homing run that physically moves
the mechanism, so it should be loaded on purpose and be removable again.
That also makes the bench procedure in TESTPLAN.md possible at all.

--- a/patches/kernel/board/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig
+++ b/patches/kernel/board/hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig
@@ -33,7 +33,10 @@
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
 # CONFIG_HY310_BOARD_MGR is not set
-# CONFIG_HY310_KEYSTONE_MOTOR is not set
+# The projector's focus stepper (motor_ctr). Module, not built-in: probe
+# arms a homing run that moves the mechanism, so it should be loaded
+# deliberately and can be unloaded again.
+CONFIG_HY310_KEYSTONE_MOTOR=m
 # CONFIG_SUNXI_NSI is not set
 # CONFIG_SUNXI_TVTOP is not set
 # DECD: the vendor AFBD frame-submission path. Built as a MODULE on purpose
